@startuml 18-er-data-model
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Segoe UI, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
skinparam ArrowFontColor #4A5568
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F59E0B
' Layer palette — byte-identical across ALL 24 diagrams
!$C_EDGE = "#2563EB"   /' frontend / edge '/
!$C_APP  = "#7C3AED"   /' orchestrator / app logic '/
!$C_GPU  = "#16A34A"   /' inference / GPU '/
!$C_DATA = "#D97706"   /' storage / data '/
!$C_EXT  = "#64748B"   /' external systems '/
!$C_RISK = "#DC2626"   /' risk / trust boundary '/

!include <tupadr3/common>
!include <tupadr3/font-awesome-5/database>
!include <tupadr3/font-awesome-5/hdd>
!include <tupadr3/font-awesome-5/search>
!include <tupadr3/font-awesome-5/exclamation_triangle>

title Entity-relationship model — three independent stores, one enforced FK graph\n(evidence: orchestrator/app/db.py:22-134, sync-worker/syncworker/storage.py:72-167, sync-worker/syncworker/rag_index.py:73-144)

skinparam class {
  BorderThickness 1
}
skinparam package {
  BorderThickness 2
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' TRUST BOUNDARY — one Docker volume holds all three stores + the SF key
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "TRUST BOUNDARY — the single Docker `data` volume\n//mounted read-write into sync-worker AND into the orchestrator that executes LLM-authored SQL (docker-compose.yml:269)//\n//it also holds the Salesforce RSA signing key at /data/sf_jwt_key.pem (syncworker/secrets.py:50)//" as VOL #back:FFFFFF;line:DC2626;line.dashed {

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' (a) app.sqlite3 — the ONLY store with declared foreign keys
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "app.sqlite3\n//stdlib sqlite3, one short-lived connection per call — db.py:195-205//\n**PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL** (db.py:201) · **PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON** (db.py:202)" as SQLITE #FFFBEB {

  entity "**users**\n//db.py:23-28//" as users #FEF3C7 {
    * **id** : INTEGER  <<PK, AUTOINCREMENT>>
    --
    * username : TEXT  <<UNIQUE, COLLATE NOCASE>>
    * password_hash : TEXT  <<literal "!local-no-login" — auth.py:79>>
    * created_at : TEXT
  }

  entity "**conversations**\n//db.py:29-37//" as conversations #FEF3C7 {
    * **id** : TEXT  <<PK — CLIENT-SUPPLIED, history.py:92>>
    --
    * //user_id// : INTEGER  <<FK → users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE>>
    * title : TEXT
    * created_at : TEXT
    * updated_at : TEXT
    * pinned : INTEGER  <<DEFAULT 0, added by migrate() db.py:141-144>>
    * archived : INTEGER  <<DEFAULT 0, added by migrate() db.py:141-144>>
  }

  entity "**messages**\n//db.py:38-51//" as messages #FEF3C7 {
    * **id** : INTEGER  <<PK, AUTOINCREMENT>>
    --
    * //conversation_id// : TEXT  <<FK → conversations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE>>
    * role : TEXT
    * content : TEXT  <<NO INDEX — LIKE full-scans at db.py:963,972,995>>
    meta : TEXT  <<JSON blob, json.loads at db.py:352>>
    * created_at : TEXT
    generation_id : TEXT  <<idempotency key, db.py:146>>
  }

  entity "**conversation_summaries**\n//db.py:55-65//" as summaries #FEF3C7 {
    * **conversation_id** : TEXT  <<PK + FK → conversations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE>>
    --
    * summary : TEXT
    * covers_through : INTEGER  <<count of folded messages>>
    * token_estimate : INTEGER
    * updated_at : TEXT
  }

  entity "**conversation_chunks**\n//db.py:69-78//" as convchunks #FEF3C7 {
    * **id** : INTEGER  <<PK, AUTOINCREMENT>>
    --
    * //conversation_id// : TEXT  <<FK → conversations(id) ON DELETE CASCADE>>
    * ordinal : INTEGER
    * role : TEXT
    * text : TEXT
    * embedding : BLOB  <<unbounded, no size cap>>
    * created_at : TEXT
    UNIQUE(conversation_id, ordinal)
  }

  entity "**uploads**\n//db.py:84-93//" as uploads #FEE2E2 {
    * **id** : TEXT  <<PK>>
    --
    * conversation_id : TEXT  <<**NO FOREIGN KEY** — db.py:86>>
    * filename : TEXT
    * bytes : INTEGER
    * status : TEXT
    profile : TEXT  <<JSON — the only data the dataset engine ever sees>>
    notes : TEXT
    * created_at : TEXT
  }

  entity "**url_documents**\n//db.py:102-110//" as urldocs #FEE2E2 {
    * **id** : INTEGER  <<PK, AUTOINCREMENT>>
    --
    * conversation_id : TEXT  <<**NO FOREIGN KEY** — db.py:104>>
    * url : TEXT
    * title : TEXT
    * text : TEXT  <<extracted readable text; source body capped at FETCH_MAX_BYTES=5 MB>>
    * fetched_at : TEXT
    UNIQUE(conversation_id, url)
  }

  entity "**repos**\n//db.py:114-122//" as repos #FEE2E2 {
    * **id** : INTEGER  <<PK, AUTOINCREMENT>>
    --
    * conversation_id : TEXT  <<**NO FOREIGN KEY** — db.py:116>>
    * repo_key : TEXT
    * url : TEXT
    * sha : TEXT  <<"" when git rev-parse fails — core/repo.py:213>>
    * cloned_at : TEXT
    UNIQUE(conversation_id, repo_key)
  }

  entity "**repo_chunks**\n//db.py:123-131//" as repochunks #FEE2E2 {
    * **id** : INTEGER  <<PK, AUTOINCREMENT>>
    --
    * conversation_id : TEXT  <<**NO FOREIGN KEY** — db.py:125>>
    * repo_key : TEXT  <<no FK to repos(repo_key) either>>
    * path : TEXT
    * start_line : INTEGER
    * end_line : INTEGER
    * text : TEXT
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' (b) DuckDB warehouse — written by sync-worker, read read-only by orchestrator
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "DuckDB warehouse\n//DUCKDB_PATH=/data/warehouse.duckdb — config.py:96, syncworker/config.py:43//\nwriter: **sync-worker** (1 conn/cycle) · reader: **orchestrator** read_only=True (schema_cache.py:40-47)" as DUCK #FFF7ED {

  entity "**<Salesforce object>**\none table per config.yaml entry\n//Account, Contact, Opportunity, Case, …//\n//created at storage.py:138-142//" as sfobj #FED7AA {
    Id : VARCHAR  <<**NO PRIMARY KEY, NO INDEX**>>
    SystemModstamp : VARCHAR
    Name : VARCHAR
    …every configured field… : VARCHAR
    --
    CREATE TABLE "obj" AS SELECT * FROM _staging_df
    ⇒ schema inferred, **every column VARCHAR**
    (normalize_records str()-casts all — storage.py:38-56)
    --
    upsert = DELETE WHERE Id IN (…) + INSERT BY NAME
    (storage.py:155-160) — **full scan per batch**
    new columns adopted by ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN
    (storage.py:151-154)
  }

  entity "**_sync_meta**\n//storage.py:80-85//" as syncmeta #FED7AA {
    * **object_name** : VARCHAR  <<PRIMARY KEY>>
    --
    watermark : VARCHAR  <<max SystemModstamp, "…Z" — storage.py:35>>
    updated_at : TIMESTAMP
    --
    written LAST, after the whole batch loop
    (syncworker/main.py:188) ⇒ crash-safe replay
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' (c) LanceDB — vector store, written by sync-worker, read by the rag engine
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "LanceDB\n//LANCEDB_DIR=/data/lancedb, LANCEDB_TABLE=chunks — config.py:97-98//" as LANCE #FFF7ED {

  entity "**chunks**\n//schema at rag_index.py:79-89//" as chunks #FED7AA {
    vector : fixed_size_list[float32, dim]  <<no PK, no unique key>>
    --
    text : string  <<one chunk of one rag_field>>
    object : string  <<Salesforce object API name>>
    record_id : string  <<15/18-char SF Id — rag_index.py:26>>
    field : string
    system_modstamp : string
    --
    write path: **delete per record_id then add**
    (rag_index.py:141-144) — one delete call PER RECORD
    read path: table.search(vec).limit(RAG_TOP_K=30)
    (rag.py:43-49)
  }
}

}
' ── end TRUST BOUNDARY ─────────────────────────────────────────────

' ── enforced foreign keys (SQLite, cascading) ──────────────────────
users        ||-[#D97706,bold]-o{ conversations : "FK user_id\n**ON DELETE CASCADE** · db.py:31"
conversations ||-[#D97706,bold]-o{ messages     : "FK conversation_id\n**ON DELETE CASCADE** · db.py:40"
conversations ||-[#D97706,bold]-|| summaries    : "FK conversation_id (also PK)\n**ON DELETE CASCADE** · db.py:56"
conversations ||-[#D97706,bold]-o{ convchunks   : "FK conversation_id\n**ON DELETE CASCADE** · db.py:71"

' ── NON-enforced, string-only associations (SQLite) ────────────────
conversations ||..[#DC2626,bold]o{ uploads     : "**conversation_id only — NO FK**\norphaned on delete · db.py:86"
conversations ||..[#DC2626,bold]o{ urldocs     : "**conversation_id only — NO FK**\norphaned on delete · db.py:104"
conversations ||..[#DC2626,bold]o{ repos       : "**conversation_id only — NO FK**\norphaned on delete · db.py:116"
conversations ||..[#DC2626,bold]o{ repochunks  : "**conversation_id only — NO FK**\norphaned on delete · db.py:125"
repos        ||..[#DC2626]o{ repochunks        : "repo_key — no FK,\nno cascade · db.py:126"

' ── cross-store, application-level joins (nothing enforces these) ──
sfobj ||..[#64748B]o{ chunks   : "Id → record_id\n//application join, rag_index.py:106-110//\nno constraint, no referential check"
sfobj ||..[#64748B]|| syncmeta : "table name → object_name\n//by convention only, syncworker/main.py:106-115//"

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' Notes
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
note bottom of uploads #FEE2E2
  **ORPHAN DEFECT — the central data-model risk.**
  `delete_conversation` executes exactly one statement:
  `DELETE FROM conversations WHERE id=? AND user_id=?`
  (**db.py:334-340**). `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON` (db.py:202)
  therefore cascades into `messages`, `conversation_summaries`
  and `conversation_chunks` — and reaches **nothing else**.

  `uploads`, `url_documents`, `repos`, `repo_chunks` declare
  `conversation_id TEXT NOT NULL` with **no REFERENCES clause**
  (db.py:86, 104, 116, 125). After the delete those rows survive
  forever: no cascade, no TTL, no pruning job anywhere in
  `orchestrator/app/` — the whole page text, code chunks and
  dataset profiles of a "deleted" chat stay readable to anyone
  who can guess or replay the conversation id.
end note

note right of messages #FFFBEB
  **Every `connect()` re-runs DDL + migration** (db.py:203-204):
  `executescript(_SCHEMA)` = 16 CREATE … IF NOT EXISTS, then
  `migrate()` runs an **unconditional** de-duplicating
  `DELETE FROM messages … GROUP BY conversation_id, generation_id`
  (db.py:181-186) — a full scan + group-by of `messages` on
  **every single database call**, with no one-time guard.

  `sqlite3.connect()` is called with **no `timeout=`** (db.py:199),
  so writes fail with "database is locked" after the stdlib
  default 5 s under contention → HTTP 500.
end note

note top of SQLITE #FFFBEB
  **Indexes — 6 declared in `_SCHEMA`:**
  1. `idx_conversation_chunks_conv` (conversation_id, ordinal) — db.py:79-80
     //redundant: UNIQUE(conversation_id, ordinal) at db.py:77 already indexes this//
  2. `idx_uploads_conversation` (conversation_id, created_at) — db.py:94-95
  3. `idx_conversations_user` (user_id, updated_at DESC) — db.py:96-97
  4. `idx_messages_conversation` (conversation_id, id) — db.py:98-99
  5. `idx_url_documents_conv` (conversation_id, id) — db.py:111-112
  6. `idx_repo_chunks_conv` (conversation_id, repo_key, id) — db.py:132-133

  **+ 1 created outside `_SCHEMA`**, in `migrate()`:
  `idx_messages_generation` UNIQUE (conversation_id, generation_id)
  WHERE generation_id IS NOT NULL — db.py:187-191 (partial, race fix)

  **No index on `messages.content`** — every conversation search is a
  full table scan (db.py:963, 972, 995).
end note

note bottom of sfobj #FEE2E2
  **DuckDB has no keys at all.** Tables are born from
  `CREATE TABLE "<obj>" AS SELECT * FROM _staging_df`
  (storage.py:138-142), which carries no PK, no UNIQUE and
  no index. Consequences:
  • `DELETE … WHERE Id IN (SELECT Id FROM _staging_df)`
    (storage.py:155-157) is a **full table scan per batch**.
  • Nothing prevents duplicate `Id` rows; correctness rests
    solely on `drop_duplicates(subset=["Id"])` (storage.py:133).
  • Every column is **VARCHAR** because `normalize_records`
    str()-casts each value (storage.py:38-56) — dates and
    amounts cannot be compared or aggregated numerically by
    the LLM-authored SQL without an explicit CAST.
  • **Salesforce deletes are never propagated** — no tombstone
    query, no `queryAll`, no reconciliation pass.
end note

note bottom of syncmeta #FFE4E6
  `_sync_meta` is created in the **`main` schema**, and
  `schema_cache` enumerates `information_schema.columns
  WHERE table_schema='main'` (schema_cache.py:47-53) — so the
  internal watermark table is handed to the SQL-writing LLM as
  if it were a business object.
end note

note bottom of chunks #FEE2E2
  **No dedup and no re-embed guard** (rag_index.py:97-154):
  the indexer never compares incoming text to what is stored —
  no content hash, no `system_modstamp` comparison. Any change
  to any field bumps `SystemModstamp`, so every long-text chunk
  of that record is re-embedded on the GPU.

  `_open_or_create_table` **ignores `dim` when the table already
  exists** (rag_index.py:77-78): switching `EMBED_MODEL` to a
  different dimension silently appends mismatched vectors.
end note

note as TRUST #FFE4E6
  **Why the dashed red boundary matters.**
  `app.sqlite3`, `warehouse.duckdb`, `lancedb/`, `parquet/` and
  the Salesforce **RSA signing key** `/data/sf_jwt_key.pem`
  (syncworker/secrets.py:50) all live in ONE Docker volume that is
  mounted into the orchestrator (docker-compose.yml:269) — the same
  container that executes LLM-authored SQL.

  The only thing separating model text from that key is the DuckDB
  connection flags: `read_only=True`, `enable_external_access=False`,
  `autoload_known_extensions=False` (sql.py:124-132), plus
  `guard_sql`'s 22-entry filesystem/network table-function blocklist
  (sql_guard.py:45-54). There is no filesystem-level isolation and no
  separate secrets mount.

  Note also that **no store enforces identity across the boundary**:
  SQLite `conversations.id` is client-supplied (history.py:92), and
  DuckDB/LanceDB carry no key at all.
end note

TRUST .[#DC2626,dashed]. VOL

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#FEF3C7> | app.sqlite3 table **with** a declared FK / cascade |
  |<#FEE2E2> | table or field carrying a data-model **risk** |
  |<#FED7AA> | analytics store (DuckDB / LanceDB) — no keys at all |
  Notation:
  `||--o{` solid orange = **enforced** FK, ON DELETE CASCADE
  `||..o{` dashed red   = column-name-only link, **no constraint**
  `||..o{` dashed grey  = cross-store join made in application code
  `*` = NOT NULL · **bold** = primary key · //italic// = foreign key
  Stores: app.sqlite3 (SQLite/WAL) · DuckDB warehouse · LanceDB.
  There is **no** cross-store transaction and no shared identity.
end legend

@enduml
